  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Diplazium esculentum",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplazium_esculentum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1378676949,
      "text": "Diplazium esculentum, the vegetable fern, is an edible fern found throughout Asia and Oceania. It is probably one of the most commonly consumed ferns."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Diplazium esculentum",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplazium_esculentum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 174538691,
      "text": "Diplazium esculentum, paca, es una especie de helecho comestible propio de Asia y Oceanía. Probablemente es la especie de helecho más consumida. En Malasia se le denomina pucuk paku y paku tanjung,  pakô en Filipinas, dhekia (ঢেকীয়া) en Assam \"Dhenkir Shaak en Bengalí, y linguda en el norte de India, en referencia a su fronda ensortijada. En Tailandia se le denomina phak khut. Si bien podría contener pequeñas cantidades de toxinas de los helechos, no existen registros de efectos tóxicos significativos."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Paku sayur",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paku_sayur",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 29966816,
      "text": "Paku sayur merupakan sejenis paku/pakis yang biasa dimakan ental mudanya sebagai sayuran oleh penduduk Asia Tenggara dan kepulauan di Samudera Pasifik. Paku ini biasanya tumbuh di tepi sungai atau di tebing-tebing yang lembap dan teduh. Pemanfaatanya biasanya digulai atau dijadikan lalap setelah direbus terlebih dahulu. Konsumsi mentah tidak dianjurkan karena mengandung asam sikimat yang mengganggu pencernaan manusia."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Diplazium esculentum § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplazium_esculentum#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1378676949,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "The young fronds are stir-fried and used in salads.\nThey may have mild amounts of fern toxins but no major toxic effects are recorded.\nIt is known as  pakô (\"wing\") in the Philippines, pucuk paku and paku tanjung in Malaysia, sayur paku or pakis in Indonesia, phak koot (Thai: ผักกูด) in Thailand, rau dớn in Vietnam, dhekia (Assamese: ঢেঁকীয়া) in Assamese, Dhenki Shaak (Bengali: ঢেঁকি শাক) in Bengali, paloi saag (Bengali: পালই শাগ) in Eastern Bengali, ningro in Nepali, dingkia in Boro and linguda in northern India, referring to the curled fronds.\nIt is known as pohole or hō'i'o in Hawaiian cuisine.\nThe ferns grow in wet areas of shady valleys. The fern species Diplazium esculentum is believed to have been introduced and naturalized in Hawaii and was first reported collected in 1910. The fern also has medicinal uses.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "es": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (es): Diplazium esculentum § Usos",
        "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplazium_esculentum#Usos",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 174538691,
        "heading": "Usos",
        "text": "Las frondas jóvenes se consumen fritas como verduras o son utilizadas en ensaladas.​​ En Hawaii se le utiliza para preparar pohole.​ A veces la planta es cultivada para decorar los hogares.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
